enterprise-grade solution that serves as an operating system. In addition, the company offers remote monitoring and management solutions that provide visibility and insights into the availability and performance of their customers' networks, infrastructure, devices, and applications through a centralized dashboard; and data protection as-a-service solutions, such as backup and disaster recovery for servers, virtual machines, workstations, files, data, and key cloud-based applications, as well as multi-tenant platform and secure remote delivery architecture. Further, it offers security services through endpoint security, managed detection and response, extended detection and response, web protection, e-mail security, and archiving solutions. Additionally, the company engages in the professional services automation, automation and scripting management, password management policies, and reporting and analytics activities. The company was incorporated in 2020 and is headquartered in Burlington, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John  Pagliuca | CEO, President & Director | Age 48 | Compensation: $934,500 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $267K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $39K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $24K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["N-able, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $951M market cap on $511M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross 